<title>UK: Russian Black Sea Novorossiisk closed by wind.</title>
<headline>Russian Black Sea Novorossiisk closed by wind.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian Black Sea oil port Novorossiisk closed again on Monday morning because of high winds and swell, a reliable shipping source said.</p>
<p>The port shut at 0630 local time.</p>
<p>Two cargoes of Urals blend crude finished loading at Novorossiisk since a previous closure last Friday morning.</p>
<p>Choktaw sailed on Friday evening with 141,000 tonnes and Arteaga with 136,000 tonnes on Sunday afternoon.</p>
<p>Black Sea terminals Odessa and Tuapse were open on Monday as was Baltic port Ventspils.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 17 542 8060</p>
